"], "rationale": "Most raters call this open, Republican-leaning seat a tossup with a slight Democratic tilt, and prediction markets price the Democrat at 55-62%. Dandiya's large cash advantage, strong third quarter, and outside support from the DCCC and Everytown, plus leaked-audio criticism of Askar, nudge the forecast modestly toward the Democrat despite the district's R+4 lean.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling or a late surge in Republican turnout across Palm Beach County could pull this back to a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 51 days old; polling uncertainty inflated."]}, "overview": "Florida's 22nd District is an open seat with a Republican-leaning partisan baseline, but most race raters call it a tossup with a slight Democratic tilt. The only two usable polls, both Democratic-sponsored and from August, showed a tied race and a two-point Democratic lead, and prediction markets price the Democrat between 55% and 62%. A favorable national environment for Democrats this cycle roughly offsets the district's Republican lean.\n\nPia Dandiya holds a clear financial edge, with about $1.1 million on hand after a $1.8 million third quarter, while Casey Askar has spent heavily of his own money and reports roughly $90,000 remaining. Democratic outside groups, including the DCCC and Everytown, are advertising against Askar, and leaked audio on data centers drew criticism. With thin, dated polling, uncertainty remains high.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5493, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5402, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4658, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4995, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5432, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5455, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5764, "margin":